  "defect_and_change": {
    "most_important": "the Skill tool never delivers skills/jev-control/SKILL.md: the command commands/jev-control.md has the same name and its text is what `Skill jev:jev-control` returns, with the model's `args` as $ARGUMENTS. The protocol (what Jev decides, the decision loop, search, done) therefore never reached the model in any of the four dev sessions of R02-R03; the model saw only the command text, the hook line and the `next` line. In d-s3b the natural-language request reached the command with no argument, step 3 ran `status`, the mode stayed off, nothing was answered (frozen oracle fails, the first failed correctness result of the campaign). In d-s3a `on` ran (the model passed args \"on\") and then the model searched with its own grep.",
    "fixed": [
      "hook.mjs: the activation line for a natural-language request now says to run `cli.mjs on --session-cap <cap> --priorities \"<one line>\"` first and to Read <plugin root>/skills/jev-control/SKILL.md; the command-prompt activation is unchanged (it must not demand `on` for off/status); the ON reminder points at skills/jev-control/SKILL.md instead of \"the jev-control skill\"",
      "commands/jev-control.md: step 1 reads SKILL.md with Read; step 3 runs `on` (not `status`) for no/unknown arguments when the hook line says the user requested the mode"
    ],
    "tests": [
      "hook.test.mjs: the natural-language activation text (on first, Read SKILL.md, the path exists), command prompts do not demand `on`, reminder text",
      "manifest.test.mjs: the command reads SKILL.md and treats a hook-requested no-argument call as `on`"
    ],
    "mutation": "both new tests fail on the HEAD versions of hook.mjs and commands/jev-control.md and pass on the new ones",
